/* Main is defined twice.  A program is a set of definitions, one per
   name, so this input is refused.  It was read with the first definition
   winning, silently, and answered sat, although the second definition
   outputs b, which q0 rejects. */
%BEGING
Main x -> e.
Main x -> b.
%ENDG

%BEGINA
q0 a -> q0.
q0 e -> .
%ENDA

%BEGINT
Main : q0 -> q0.
%ENDT
